Split the integral where the formula changes.
$\begin{align*}\int_{-3}^0 k(3+x)\,dx+\int_0^3 k(3-x)\,dx&=1\\k\left[3x+\frac{x^2}{2}\right]_{-3}^0+k\left[3x-\frac{x^2}{2}\right]_0^3&=1\\\frac{9k}{2}+\frac{9k}{2}&=1\\9k&=1\\k&=\frac{1}{9}\end{align*}$
The sketch shows the two pieces meeting at height $3k=\frac{1}{3}$. Both pieces are nonnegative.
